class Solution {

    public ListNode reverseLinkedList(ListNode head) { //Reversing the list iteratively

        ListNode temp = head;                   // Start from the head of the list
        ListNode prev = null;                   // Previous node is initially null

        while (temp != null) {                  // Traverse the linked list

            ListNode front = temp.next;         // Store the next node before breaking the link

            temp.next = prev;                   // Reverse the current node's link

            prev = temp;                        // Move prev one step forward

            temp = front;                       // Move temp to the next node
        }

        return prev;                            // Prev becomes the new head of the reversed list
    }

    public boolean isPalindrome(ListNode head) {  // MAIN FUNCTION

        ListNode slow = head;                   // Slow pointer starts from head
        ListNode fast = head;                   // Fast pointer starts from head

        while (fast.next != null && fast.next.next != null) { // Find the middle of the linked list
            slow = slow.next;                   // Move slow by one step
            fast = fast.next.next;              // Move fast by two steps
        }

        ListNode newHead = reverseLinkedList(slow.next); // Reverse the second half of the list

        ListNode first = head;                  // Pointer for the first half
        ListNode second = newHead;              // Pointer for the reversed second half

        while (second != null) {                // Compare both halves

            if (first.val != second.val) {      // If values are different, not a palindrome

                reverseLinkedList(newHead);     // Restore the original linked list

                return false;                   // Return false
            }

            first = first.next;                 // Move first pointer

            second = second.next;               // Move second pointer
        }

        reverseLinkedList(newHead);             // Restore the original linked list

        return true;                            // All values matched, it is a palindrome
    }
}

Palindrome in Linked List (Optimal)

1. Find the middle using Slow & Fast pointers.
2. Reverse the second half.
3. Compare first half and reversed second half.
4. Restore the second half.
5. Return the result.

Time Complexity  : O(n)   // Find middle O(n/2) + Reverse O(n/2) + Compare O(n/2) + Restore O(n/2) = O(2n)
Space Complexity : O(1)   // Only pointers are used, no extra data structure
